1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--categories-of-language-difficulty","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/categories-of-language-difficulty","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/categories-of-language-difficulty","sourceHash":"35bae963a979c598e377e100fa10516c0b0f2b23078fa21b95e804c5cadd32e3","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T16:52:34.798Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Categories of Language Difficulty","zh":"语言难度分类"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"All languages, in isolation, are the same difficulty to learn. There are no natural languages that babies can't learn just as well as others. But as adult language learners who already speak at least one other language, certain languages will be easier or harder to learn.","zh":"单独来看，所有语言的学习难度都相同。不存在婴儿无法像学习其他语言一样学会的自然语言。不过，成年语言学习者已经会说至少一种语言，因此某些语言对他们来说会更容易或更难学习。"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"\"Easier or harder\" isn't exactly the right way to put it. Learning a language is like a marathon — even a marathon on a nice flat track is still a very long distance to run and most people can't do that without training. But some languages have specific features that make them harder (or easier) to pick up, just as certain race courses have different features.","zh":"用“更容易或更难”来形容其实并不完全准确。学习一门语言就像跑马拉松——即使是在平坦舒适的赛道上，马拉松的距离依然很长，大多数人不经过训练都无法完成。不过，某些语言具有一些特征，会让掌握它们变得更难（或更容易），就像不同的马拉松路线各有特点一样。"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Not only are the race tracks different, but you may or may not have a head start. Imagine running a marathon, but starting halfway down the course — that'd be much easier than doing the whole thing wearing ankle weights. This part of the metaphor represents the languages you already speak. The more similar your native language is to your target language, the more of a head start you have.","zh":"不仅赛道各不相同，你还可能拥有或没有领先优势。想象一下跑马拉松时从赛程中点出发——这显然比全程戴着脚踝负重跑容易得多。这个比喻中的领先优势代表你已经会说的语言。你的母语与目标语言越相似，你的起步优势就越大。"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"One of the hardest parts about learning a language is the sheer number of words you need to know. But English and French share a huge number of very similar words — about 60% of all the words in a contemporary French novel are cognates with English words. In a Japanese text, that number is almost 0%.","zh":"学习语言最困难的部分之一，是需要掌握的词汇数量极其庞大。但英语和法语共享大量非常相似的词汇——当代法语小说中约 60% 的词与英语词同源。而在日语文本中，这一比例几乎为 0%。"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"We separate languages (roughly) into 4 groups, depending on how different they are from your native language. Since Refold is a primarily English-speaking company, we use English as the native language for these calculations. If you speak a different native language, your version of this chart will look very different. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/how-long-does-it-take-to-learn-a-language\">How Long Does It Take to Learn a Language</a>","zh":"我们根据目标语言与母语之间的差异程度，将语言大致分为 4 类。由于 Refold 主要面向英语使用者，我们在计算时以英语作为母语。如果你的母语不是英语，这张图表对你来说会有很大不同。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/how-long-does-it-take-to-learn-a-language\">学会一门语言需要多长时间</a>"}},{"id":"similar-languages","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Similar Languages","zh":"相似语言"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"These are languages that have a common ancestor with English. You have a large head start because you share a lot of vocabulary, grammar features, and sometimes even sounds with your target language.","zh":"这类语言与英语拥有共同的祖先。由于目标语言与英语共享大量词汇、语法特征，有时甚至连语音也很相似，因此你拥有很大的起步优势。"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Many Germanic and Romance languages fall into this category for English speakers:","zh":"对英语使用者而言，许多日耳曼语族和罗曼语族语言都属于这一类："}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Spanish, French, Italian, Portuguese","zh":"西班牙语、法语、意大利语、葡萄牙语"},{"en":"German, Dutch, Swedish, Norwegian","zh":"德语、荷兰语、瑞典语、挪威语"}]},{"id":"other-languages","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Other Languages","zh":"其他语言"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Most of the 7,000+ languages in the world fall into this category. The marathon track isn't particularly challenging, but you don't start with the big head start of knowing thousands of similar words.","zh":"世界上 7,000 多种语言中的大多数都属于这一类。马拉松赛道本身并没有特别困难，但你也没有预先掌握数千个相似词汇所带来的巨大起步优势。"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"If your target language isn't in the Similar or Distant categories, it's probably here. Some examples:","zh":"如果你的目标语言既不属于相似语言，也不属于远距离语言，那么它很可能属于这一类。例如："}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Russian, Czech, Polish","zh":"俄语、捷克语、波兰语"},{"en":"Greek, Finnish, Hebrew","zh":"希腊语、芬兰语、希伯来语"},{"en":"Hindi, Tagalog, Swahili","zh":"印地语、他加禄语、斯瓦希里语"},{"en":"Indonesian, Thai, Vietnamese","zh":"印度尼西亚语、泰语、越南语"}]},{"id":"distant-languages","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Distant Languages","zh":"远距离语言"}},{"id":"segment-0015","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Some of the biggest languages in the world have both a difficult and complicated race course <em>and</em> features that make them especially hard for English speakers.","zh":"世界上一些使用人数最多的语言，不仅有困难而复杂的赛道，<em>还</em>具有一些令英语使用者格外难以掌握的特征。"}},{"id":"segment-0016","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Japanese and Korean are notorious for having a fundamentally different sentence structure from European languages. Arabic changes and morphs words in ways that take a long time for English speakers to get used to. Mandarin uses \"tones\" — just the tone you pronounce a word with can change its meaning from <em>horse</em> to <em>mother</em>.","zh":"日语和韩语以句子结构与欧洲语言存在根本差异而闻名。阿拉伯语会以各种方式改变词形，英语使用者需要很长时间才能习惯。普通话使用“声调”——仅仅改变一个词的声调，就可能让它的意思从<em>马</em>变成<em>妈</em>。"}},{"id":"segment-0017","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"There aren't many truly distant languages, but the common ones are:","zh":"真正的远距离语言并不多，但常见的有："}},{"id":"segment-0018","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Japanese, Korean","zh":"日语、韩语"},{"en":"Mandarin, Cantonese (and other Chinese languages)","zh":"普通话、粤语（以及其他汉语变体）"},{"en":"Arabic (and its dialects)","zh":"阿拉伯语（及其方言）"}]},{"id":"cousin-languages","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Cousin Languages","zh":"近亲语言"}},{"id":"segment-0020","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"There's also a category even easier than \"similar\" — cousin languages. These are very closely related languages that share over 50% (often way more) of their vocabulary and have very similar sentence structures and grammar.","zh":"还有一类比“相似”更容易的语言——近亲语言。这些语言之间关系非常密切，共享超过 50%（通常远高于此）的词汇，并且句子结构和语法也极为相似。"}},{"id":"segment-0021","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"For English speakers, this category is essentially empty (Scots and Frisian, basically). But for speakers of other languages, it's very relevant. If you speak Spanish, then Italian, Portuguese, French, and Catalan are all cousin languages. If you speak Russian, then Ukrainian, Polish, Czech, and Slovak are cousins.","zh":"对英语使用者而言，这一类别基本是空的（大致只有低地苏格兰语和弗里斯兰语）。但对其他语言的使用者来说，这一类别非常重要。如果你会说西班牙语，那么意大利语、葡萄牙语、法语和加泰罗尼亚语都是它的近亲语言。如果你会说俄语，那么乌克兰语、波兰语、捷克语和斯洛伐克语就是它的近亲语言。"}},{"id":"it-depends-on-you-too","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"It Depends on You, Too","zh":"这也取决于你自己"}},{"id":"segment-0023","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Language distance is the biggest factor, but it's not the only one. Your experience matters a lot. If you've already learned two other foreign languages as an adult, you're going to have a much easier time with a third one, even if it's distant. You already understand your personal learning process and have experienced a lot of the pitfalls.","zh":"语言距离是最重要的因素，但不是唯一因素。你的经验也非常重要。如果成年后已经学过另外两门外语，那么学习第三门语言会轻松得多，即便它是一门远距离语言。你已经了解适合自己的学习过程，也经历过许多常见的陷阱。"}},{"id":"segment-0024","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"If you have experience with a language related to your target language, that helps enormously. An English speaker who's fluent in Spanish will have a much easier time learning Italian than a monolingual English speaker.","zh":"如果你接触过与目标语言相关的语言，也会有极大帮助。一位能流利使用西班牙语的英语母语者，学习意大利语会比只会英语的人轻松得多。"}},{"id":"approximate-hours-to-functional-fluency","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Approximate Hours to Functional Fluency","zh":"达到功能性流利所需的大致小时数"}},{"id":"segment-0026","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"These numbers assume you're using an immersion-based method and are meant as rough planning estimates: <a href=\"/roadmap/library/functional-fluency\">Functional Fluency</a>","zh":"以下数字假设你使用以沉浸为基础的方法，仅作为粗略的规划估算：<a href=\"/roadmap/library/functional-fluency\">功能性流利</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0027","type":"table","rows":[[{"en":"Category","zh":"类别","header":true},{"en":"Hours to Functional Fluency","zh":"达到功能性流利所需小时数","header":true}],[{"en":"Cousin language","zh":"近亲语言","header":false},{"en":"~800","zh":"约 800","header":false}],[{"en":"Similar language","zh":"相似语言","header":false},{"en":"~1,350","zh":"约 1,350","header":false}],[{"en":"Other language","zh":"其他语言","header":false},{"en":"~1,700","zh":"约 1,700","header":false}],[{"en":"Distant language","zh":"远距离语言","header":false},{"en":"~2,700","zh":"约 2,700","header":false}]]},{"id":"segment-0028","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"These are based on the Foreign Service Institute's decades of experience, modified to better match the experience of our immersion learning community. For a full breakdown by phase, see the article on how long it takes to learn a language. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/how-long-does-it-take-to-learn-a-language\">How Long Does It Take to Learn a Language</a>","zh":"这些数字以美国外交学院数十年的经验为基础，并经过调整，以更贴合我们沉浸学习社区的实际经验。有关各阶段所需时间的完整细分，请参阅“学会一门语言需要多长时间”一文。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/how-long-does-it-take-to-learn-a-language\">学会一门语言需要多长时间</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0029","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Keep in mind that \"language distance\" isn't meant to be a perfect, objective measurement. All language pairs have their own nuance. But these groupings are useful for planning your learning journey and setting realistic expectations.","zh":"请记住，“语言距离”并不是一种完美、客观的衡量标准。每一对语言都有各自的细微差异。不过，这些分类有助于规划你的学习旅程，并设定切合实际的预期。"}},{"id":"research-and-reasoning","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Research and Reasoning","zh":"研究与论证"}},{"id":"segment-0031","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The language categories used here are adapted from the Foreign Service Institute (FSI), which groups languages into 4 categories based on how long English-speaking diplomats take to reach professional working proficiency. We've adjusted these categories slightly — adding \"cousin languages\" (since the FSI doesn't distinguish them separately) and regrouping some languages based on the experience of immersion learners, who have a somewhat different time profile from classroom learners.","zh":"此处使用的语言分类改编自美国外交学院（FSI）的分类体系。该体系根据以英语为母语的外交官达到专业工作熟练度所需的时间，将语言分为四类。我们对这些类别做了少量调整——增加了“近亲语言”（因为 FSI 并未将其单独区分），并根据沉浸学习者的经验重新归类了部分语言，因为他们的学习时间曲线与课堂学习者有所不同。"}},{"id":"segment-0032","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The concept of language transfer — that your native language affects how quickly you learn a new one — is well-established in SLA research (Odlin, 1989). Positive transfer (cognates, shared grammar) gives you a head start with similar languages, while negative transfer (false friends, conflicting structures) can slow you down with distant ones. The claim about French-English cognates is supported by corpus linguistics research showing high lexical overlap between the two languages due to their shared history.","zh":"语言迁移是指母语会影响你学习一门新语言的速度，这一概念已在第二语言习得（SLA）研究中得到充分确立（Odlin，1989）。正迁移（同源词、相同的语法）会让你在学习相似语言时更有优势，而负迁移（假同源词、相冲突的结构）则可能拖慢你学习差异较大语言的速度。关于法语和英语同源词的说法也得到了语料库语言学研究的支持：由于两种语言共享一段历史，它们在词汇上有很高的重合度。"}}],"cards":[]}}]
